                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_409">Norwich, Norfolk.
                        Carmelite convent</orgName><p>Notes connect the book with the Carmelites
                        and in particular the Norwich convent: (fol. 191v) "Orate pro anima [...]
                        Thome Bradley quondam anachorit' in Conuentu fratrum Carmelitarum norwic'",
                        and on fol. 166v: "Doctor waterpytte [Th. Waterpytte, prior c. 1486--1491]
                        dedit Ricardo Cakure istum librum".</p><p>Later inscriptions seem to relate
                        to the cathedral priory: (fol. 69r) "Iste codex pertinet ad me D. Georgium
                        Canky [?] monacum Norwycensis ad me Dompne George iste liber
                     pertinet."</p></provenance>
               </history>
